<article class="env-lemma" id="07IA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07IA">Lemma <span data-tag="07IA">60.8.3</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/07MF" data-tag="07MF">60.7.5</a>. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ (U_3, T_3, \delta _3) \ar[d] \ar[r] &  (U_2, T_2, \delta _2) \ar[d] \\  (U_1, T_1, \delta _1) \ar[r] &  (U, T, \delta ) }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a fibre square in the category of divided power thickenings of $X$ relative to $(S, \mathcal{I}, \gamma )$. If $T_2 \to T$ is flat and $U_2 = T_2 \times _ T U$, then $T_3 = T_1 \times _ T T_2$ (as schemes). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because a divided power structure extends uniquely along a flat ring map. See Divided Power Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/07H1" data-tag="07H1">23.4.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>